A-DL-59 dl59-join: per-theap PAGE SLACK vs invisible per-worker slope (m90 census)
grade=ADVISORY  # analysis on already-consumed m90 raws; lane carries the declared
                # selection-mismatch caveats of repair90 (A-BB65); VERDICT-grade only
                # via the future barrier channel A-DL-57/58
inputs: 20 committed raws wp78-harness/measure-out/m90.slope.w{4,8,12,16}.r{1..5}.a1.memcensus
        + wp91-harness/repair90-estimators.out (authority for invisible slope/intercept)
machine truth (parsed from repair90-estimators.out, not hardcoded):
  slope_invisible=4480174 B/worker  intercept_invisible=71934811 B
  slope_vis=15777004 B/worker  a_vis=692184  marginal_ratio_vs_b_peak_median=0.778

row grammar found (field names per NOME):
  tag=mi_bin thr=<k> src=tls size=<bin> reserved= committed= used_b= used_n= areas=
    (NO ckpt= field on these rows; attribution below)
  tag=peak_self thr=<k> ckpt=peak_inreq alloc_id=memcount-v2-s82   # dump announcement
  tag=mi_bin_thr_sum thr=<k> heap=<ptr> reserved= committed= used_b=  # per-thread SUM of
    its tls rows; SAME heap ptr and SAME committed for every thr => the tls dumps are
    per-thread VIEWS of the ONE shared heap (arena json: heaps=1, theaps=W+extras)
  tag=mi_theap_pages ... ckpt=<c> heap=0 pages= committed= used_blocks= free_pages= free_committed=
    (+ trailer heaps_total=1 heap_overflow=0 declared=heap-by-visit-index,noalloc-visitors-A-MS50)
  tag=mi_theap_bin ... ckpt=<c> heap=0 bin=<b> free_pages= free_committed=

chosen checkpoint (per NOME): ckpt=peak_inreq, per-thread tls dump #1
  There is NO per-thread tls dump at ckpt=peak_inreq_pwork: each thread emits exactly TWO
  tls dumps per run — dump#1 announced by 'tag=peak_self thr=k ckpt=peak_inreq' (between the
  tag=peak_inreq_pwork summary row and the 'mi_proc win=9 ckpt=peak_inreq' marker), and
  dump#2 just before tag=exit (exit-side). dump#1 = the WORK-side in-request-peak snapshot,
  a few hundred ms after pwork with near-identical commit — the closest snapshot to the
  pwork window on which the invisible slope was estimated (VCOV A-BG57, 'pooled OLS of
  pwork-commit minus vis'). dump#2 is reported as a control column.
  ATTRIBUTION rule: last-seen-ckpt is unreliable (peak_self rows poison it; writer
  interleaving differs across raws). Rule used per NOME: per-thread TEMPORAL order — each
  thread's tls rows are split at the first repeated size class into dump#1 / dump#2;
  positional sanity (d1 before / d2 after the 'mi_proc win=9 ckpt=peak_inreq' marker) is
  verified and printed per run.

SLACK formulas (per NOME, declared):
  SLACK_naive(run)  = sum over thr=0..W-1, over size classes, of (committed - used_b)
                      from tag=mi_bin src=tls dump#1 rows  [the task's literal formula]
  SLACK_global(run) = mean over thr of Sum_size (committed - used_b) of that thr's dump#1
                      [deduplicated: the tls dumps all describe the ONE shared heap, so the
                       naive Sum over thr counts the same heap W times — see refutation]
  free_committed of retained pages is NOT a field on src=tls rows; retained fully-free
  pages (page_full_retain=2) stay committed with used_b=0 and land in (committed-used_b)
  (rows with used_n=0 & committed>0 are counted per run below). The explicit free_committed
  fields (mi_theap_pages/mi_theap_bin) cover ONLY the single visited heap (heaps_total=1,
  noalloc-visitor A-MS50/KL-90-3); the visited-heap value at pwork is an advisory column.

