anomalies per NOME (flagged runs of repair90 A-BB67 seen through SLACK):
  w4.r1: SLACK_global=1,992,668 (sisters 1,995,900..2,046,348)  pwork_commit=151,781,376 (sisters 153,681,920..154,009,600)
  w12.r3: SLACK_global=5,029,297 (sisters 4,949,985..4,956,061)  pwork_commit=303,431,680 (sisters 324,993,024..334,561,280)
  w16.r1: SLACK_global=6,887,306 (sisters 6,876,406..6,956,674)  pwork_commit=399,638,528 (sisters 389,611,520..390,856,704)
  - w4.r1: low pair with w4.r5 in SLACK_global (-2.5% vs the r2..r4 cluster) and lowest
    pwork_commit (-1.4%); mild in SLACK — its A-BB67 outlier flag is not slack-driven.
  - w12.r3: HIGHEST SLACK_global of its W (+1.6%) while its pwork_commit is ~25-30MB BELOW
    the sisters: the run is an outlier in the invisible (arena-level) mass, in the opposite
    direction of its slack — further evidence slack and invisible mass are different bodies.
  - w16.r1: unremarkable in SLACK (mid-pack). All W=16 runs (only they) show the retained
    free pages: 16 view-rows x 262,144 B = 4,194,304 B naive (262,144 B deduplicated).

VERDICT (ADVISORY): the page-slack hypothesis does NOT hold.
  - The task-literal Sum-over-theaps SLACK_naive gives slope ~1.9x the invisible slope with
    a NEGATIVE intercept (wrong shape AND wrong sign), but it is invalid per NOME: the tls
    dumps are W per-thread views of one shared heap (identical heap ptr + identical
    committed across thr; Sum_thr committed >> process commit).
  - The physical (deduplicated) SLACK_global slope is ~9% of the invisible slope: page
    slack cannot be 'first explanation' of the invisible per-worker slope.
  - Decisive identity: vis_model(W) == heap bin-committed (<0.5%): bin page slack is
    already counted INSIDE the census coverage; the invisible mass = pwork_commit - vis
    sits at arena/chunk level, outside the bins the slack lives in.
